==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|übertragen}}, at least in part a {{cal|de|la|transfero|transferre|nocap=1}}. Analysable as {{prefix|de|über|t1=over|tragen|t2=to carry}}. Compare {{cog|nl|overdragen}}, {{m+|en|carry over}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˌyːbərˈtraːɡən/|[ˌʔyːbɐˈtʁaːɡn̩]|[-ɡən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-übertragen.ogg|Audio}}
* {{hyphenation|de|über|tra|gen}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=6|überträgt|übertrug|übertragen|past subjunctive=übertrüge}}

# to [[transfer]], [[transmit]]
# to [[translate]]
# to [[broadcast]], [[televise]]
# to [[hand over]] something to somebody, [[entrust]] somebody with something, [[confer]] a right on somebody
# {{lb|de|medicine}} to have a post-term [[birth]]
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to be passed on to somebody (''disease, illness'')
# {{lb|de|reflexive|figuratively}} to communicate itself to somebody (''enthusiasm, nervousness, etc.)

